  "summary": "A centrifugal pump designed to be installed directly in a straight pipe run: suction and discharge flanges face each other on one centreline. Liquid enters horizontally, turns upward into the eye of the vertical-shaft impeller, is discharged into the volute and turned back to the outlet flange. The vertical motor sits on a lantern above; a spacer coupling lets the seal be changed without disturbing the motor. Small footprint, common in HVAC, water and process plants.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Rotodynamic (centrifugal), radial flow",
    "configuration": "Vertical inline, overhung",
    "api_610_type": "OH3 (bearing bracket), OH4 (rigidly coupled), OH5 (close-coupled); model shows OH4-style rigid coupling"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "impeller": "Closed radial, 6 blades",
    "seal": "Cartridge mechanical seal",
    "motor": "Vertical flange-mounted (thrust carried by motor bearings)"
  },
